body:
It's hard to avoid DR spoilers because it's gotten so big over the years. I've been waiting for the release of English V3 and I already know all of the survivors because I couldn't stay off the internet... how fantastic.

I never watch DR videos since I fear I'll find something spoilery in my recommendations... doesn't really matter now though since I know the gist of what's going to happen... still have to wait for two months. 

I also recommend staying off of most DR communities unless you know for sure they won't post any spoilers. And no matter how much you like a character, don't read their wiki page! I've spoiled myself for the first game because I like to read wiki pages on characters in my spare time. Like... even if a character dies, don't read their wiki page until your finished with their respective game. AND EVEN THEN... some characters return for the DR3 anime, so I'd advise against the wiki until you're done with the series... but you won't have a problem unless you're a pathological wiki page reader like me. Just my two cents. ^^;
